  "term": "coefficient of concordance",
  "definition": "The coefficient of concordance is a statistic used to show how much agreement there is among multiple raters when they judge items on an ordered scale, such as a five-point rating scale. In this context, higher values indicate greater consistency in the raters’ evaluations.",
